# Documentation

Write repository files in English: code, comments, docs, ADRs, plans, and log messages.

Update the README when commands, setup, or the public structure change.

Write an ADR only for a decision a newcomer could reasonably take the other way. Do not write an ADR for a rule this repository already mandates.

ADRs live in `docs/adr/NNNN-decision-name.md` and use these sections: Status, Context, Decision, Consequences.

Plans live in `docs/plans/` and record objective, context, scope, non-scope, steps, risks, and validation.

```markdown
# Title

## Status

Accepted

## Context

## Decision

## Consequences
```
